# K0 / B008 — Run 2 replica annotation (blind).

C R199 OL WF-010,WF-003 | MUST | Code review examines the actual changed behavior and reports concrete defects or risks; it is not the completion checklist — verify runs the final build/test/diff verification. | Code review | none stated
C R200 OL WF-011 | MUST | Prioritize findings: correctness; security and authorization; data integrity and persistence; architectural boundary violations; concurrency and integration; missing meaningful tests; maintainability; credible performance; do not elevate style above defects or bury important findings. | Code review | none stated
C R201 OL WF-001,WF-010 | MUST | Establish the reviewed scope, read changed code plus callers/contracts/dependencies (never isolated lines), identify intended behavior and tests, read the standards for touched scopes and load the knowledge skill for each changed technology area. | Code review | none stated
C R202 OL GOV-003,GOV-006,GOV-001,GOV-005 | MUST | Check specification conformance in both directions (approved CUSTOM_SETTINGS values are intended behavior): flag missing/weakened required behavior and unapproved product behavior (new limits, reserved names/values, observable string-comparison semantics incl. database configuration/framework defaults, new required fields, extra workflow restrictions, extra user-visible validation); approved recorded details are not drift; internal details are not product behavior. | Code review | approved recorded details
C R203 OL WF-012 | MUST | Look for correctness defects (conditions, state transitions, null/empty, async/cancellation, error mapping, lifetimes, side effects, races) and report a failure only with a plausible execution path. | Code review | none stated
C R204 OL WF-011,GOV-012,ARC-020 | MUST | Check backend changes against the architecture standard (Domain independence, Application free of Infrastructure/EF Core, thin Controllers, Application Services, specific repositories, no DbContext/DbSet/IQueryable leaks, no independent repository commits, IUnitOfWork commit boundary), proportionality (no unapproved Rich Domain, DDD, CQRS/MediatR/VSA, extra layers, project-wide Result) and frontend changes against the Angular standard without applying backend project-boundary rules mechanically. | Code review | none stated
C R205 OL WF-012 | MUST NOT | Do not report a violation merely because the implementation differs from a pattern the project has not adopted; do not require unadopted patterns (MediatR, CQRS, VSA, Minimal APIs, Rich Domain Models, Domain Events, generic repositories). | Code review | none stated
C R206 OL WF-007,PST-008 | MUST | When relevant check commit/transaction behavior, destructive changes, raw SQL parameterization, authorization, trust boundaries, secrets, sensitive logging, concurrency, migrations and cache consistency against the standards, and the seeder obligation for model/migration changes affecting seeded entities; use the full security-scan only for a requested audit, a materially security-sensitive change or a concrete finding. | Code review | none stated
C R207 OL RUN-016,WF-011 | MUST NOT | Check external calls for cancellation, time limits, idempotency, retry safety, failure translation and lifetime; do not demand retries for operations that are not safe to retry. | Code review | none stated
C R208 OL TST-009,TST-010,TST-011 | MUST | Check that changed behavior has useful maintained coverage; for bug fixes look for the regression test; confirm probe preservation; do not demand duplicate tests when equivalent coverage exists. | Code review | equivalent coverage
C R209 OL WF-011,RUN-008 | MUST NOT | Report performance only with a credible reason; do not recommend compiled queries, pooling, caching, ValueTask or similar optimizations speculatively. | Code review | none stated
C R210 OL WF-021 | MUST NOT | Review needs no MCP server or specific analyzer; tool output is evidence, not authority — read the code before turning a warning into a finding. | Code review | none stated
C R211 OL WF-011 | MUST | Each finding states severity, location, what is wrong, why it matters and the smallest fix, ordered by severity (Critical, High, Medium, Low). | Code review output | none stated
C R212 OL WF-012 | MUST NOT | Do not manufacture findings to populate categories; with no meaningful findings say so and name important unverifiable areas; no filler praise. | Code review output | none stated
C R213 OL WF-010,WF-011,WF-012 | MUST NOT | Review discipline: do not rewrite working code during review unless asked, report tooling-owned formatting, demand personal style preferences or assume every warning is a bug. | Code review | explicit request
C R214 OL GOV-010,RUN-015 | MUST | Numbers in configuration examples are illustrative; choose retry counts, timeouts and limits from actual integration and deployment requirements. | Backend configuration | none stated
C R215 OL GOV-010 | REQUIRES_APPROVAL | A new or changed setting not already defined by the specification or approved behavior must be confirmed as approved; otherwise raise a Decision Request first. | custom-settings | none stated
C R216 OL GOV-009 | REQUIRES_APPROVAL | Check SPECIFICATION.md for conflicts before synchronizing a setting. | custom-settings | none stated
C R217 OL GOV-008,GOV-011 | MUST | Record the setting with a stable descriptive name and purpose; do not record framework defaults the project has not intentionally overridden. | custom-settings | none stated
C R218 OL GOV-021 | MUST | Search for the old value, setting name, validators/DTO constraints, Domain/Application checks, mapping constraints, frontend validation/UI hints, tests/test data, docs/examples and mirrored configuration; separate coincidences; update every affected implementation, validation, configuration, test, documentation and mirrored frontend/backend surface, preferring one normal source over duplicated literals. | custom-settings | unrelated numeric coincidences
C R219 OL FE-010 | MUST | Where frontend and backend expose the same constraint, backend validation stays authoritative and frontend validation/messages follow it for UX. | custom-settings | none stated
C R220 OL PST-009 | MUST | When a setting change affects schema constraints, indexes, column lengths or other persistence metadata: update the EF Core mapping, create the appropriate migration per the migration workflow (edit an uncommitted migration only when normal; never casually alter existing migrations), verify Development seeding remains valid and update provider-sensitive tests when needed. | Schema-affecting settings | none stated
C R221 OL GOV-021,GOV-009,WF-003 | MUST | Verify settings changes: search for stale references, build affected backend/frontend, run relevant tests, verify persistence changes, re-check SPECIFICATION.md, run verify; changing one literal alone does not establish synchronization and the setting is not declared synchronized until every surface is updated and verified. | custom-settings | none stated
C R222 OL DEP-018 | MUST NOT | Containers are optional (D-14): introduce Docker or container publishing only when the project has adopted containers. | Delivery changes | none stated
C R223 OL WF-001,GOV-013 | MUST | Inspect what actually exists before writing pipeline or container files; do not assume PostgreSQL, Redis, Docker or frontend tooling; add stages for the actual project, not generic boilerplate. | delivery-pipeline | none stated
C R224 OL WF-017 | MUST | CI definitions are kept in source control, reproduce the repository's supported build and test commands and never hide build or test failures (no suppressed or skipped failing tests to permit deployment). | CI pipelines | none stated
C R225 OL WF-018 | MUST | Frontend CI uses scripts that exist in package.json (never invented) and npm ci whenever a maintained lockfile supports it, not reflexive npm install. | Frontend CI | none stated
C R226 OL WF-019,PST-004 | MUST NOT | Production database migrations are not applied automatically from normal startup by default; a production migration is an explicit, controlled deployment step with approved credentials that fails visibly (scripts/bundles may be generated earlier in CI); Development seeding never runs in Production. | Deployment | none stated
C R227 OL WF-017,WF-004,WF-006 | MUST | Verify a pipeline: restore from a clean environment, build backend and frontend (when present), run configured tests, no developer-machine state, no exposed secrets, expected artifacts; for container changes build the image, start the app and check port/configuration, non-root execution and health-probe integration. | delivery-pipeline | none stated
C X27 EX WF-009 | MUST | The delivery-pipeline output lists files changed, stages and the commands they run, what was verified and any hosting-platform assumption still needing confirmation. | End of delivery-pipeline | none stated | Workflow-specific report content beyond WF-009's verification reporting. | The report must name unconfirmed hosting assumptions.
C R228 OL GOV-012,GOV-013,ARC-007 | DEFAULT | Use interface-to-implementation registration at architectural boundaries (concrete registration for implementation-only helpers); prefer explicit registration in small/medium applications; keyed services, factories, decorators, Scrutor and convention scanning only for actual composition problems (Scrutor not for a single decoration; scan the owning assembly). | Backend DI | actual composition problem
C R229 OL GOV-002 | MUST | For a new application or substantial feature read SPECIFICATION.md before planning or implementing, and CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md when it holds values. | development-workflow | none stated
C R230 OL GOV-018,GOV-004,GOV-006,GOV-010 | MUST | Check the request against the challenge obligation and the product-source rules (gaps, string semantics, tunable values) before implementing. | development-workflow | none stated
C R231 OL WF-001 | MUST | Inspect the relevant existing code (code, callers, contracts, tests, conventions) before any non-trivial change; apply standards and knowledge for touched areas; when planning before files are opened, read the standards for the scopes to be changed; load the knowledge skill for each technology involved; route sub-tasks to their workflows. | development-workflow | none stated
C R232 OL GOV-014 | MUST | Stay within the requested scope. | Implementation | none stated
C R233 OL TST-009 | DEFAULT | For a meaningful bug with plausible recurrence add a regression test that fails before and passes after the fix, unless equivalent coverage exists. | Bug fixes | equivalent coverage
C R234 OL PST-008,PST-006 | MUST | Whenever a Domain or persistence change affects seeded entities (new required/removed/renamed properties, changed relationships, required related entities, enum/status values, meaningful states, invariants) update the development seeder in the same change; recreating an empty Development database must yield valid representative data; already seeded rows are not patched. | Persistence/model changes | none stated
C R235 OL PST-010,PST-008 | MUST | Treat EF Core migrations as source code: review every generated migration before committing (destructive changes, column recreation, data migrations, indexes, foreign keys, delete behavior) and review the seeder together with any migration affecting seeded entities. | Migrations | none stated
C R236 OL RUN-012 | MUST | Performance-motivated changes: identify the bottleneck, preserve behavior, simplest effective optimization, add/maintain tests, benchmark or profile non-obvious/complex optimizations. | Performance changes | none stated
C R237 OL API-014,GOV-017 | REQUIRES_APPROVAL | Classify a public API contract change as compatible or breaking; a breaking change to a relied-on contract follows the versioning rules and is Reserved. | Public API changes | none stated
C R238 OL API-022 | MUST | Deprecating an externally consumed API version: mark it in versioning metadata, document the replacement, communicate a realistic migration and removal timeline, keep the old version working for the promised period, and do not remove it without considering the published support contract. | API deprecation | none stated
C R239 OL WF-002 | MUST | For substantial feature work or a newly implemented application run code-review (agent code-reviewer) before final verification. | development-workflow | none stated
C R240 OL WF-003,WF-007 | MUST | Before declaring implementation complete run verify with checks appropriate to scope and risk. | development-workflow | none stated
C X28 EX WF-009,GOV-017 | MUST | The development-workflow output states what changed and why, the Delegated decisions taken, Decision Requests raised or still unresolved, and the verification report. | End of implementation work | none stated | WF-009 covers verification reporting; reporting every Delegated decision taken and every Decision Request is an additional duty. | An implementation summary must list the Delegated decisions the agent made.

